  "verbalization": "Idarubicin is associated with Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia through a pathway involving Decitabine, which is indicated in multiple genetic subtypes of Acute Myeloid Leukemia. The evidence suggests that Idarubicin may be repurposed for treating this condition, as it shares a common indication with Decitabine in various genetic profiles of Acute Myeloid Leukemia. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Idarubicin and the disease, with Decitabine acting as a bridge in the pathway. The recurring association with Decitabine implies a potential mechanism of action that is relevant across different genetic subtypes of Acute Myeloid Leukemia. The integration of these paths highlights the role of Decitabine in the treatment of this condition, suggesting that Idarubicin may be a viable candidate for repurposing in inherited forms of Acute Myeloid Leukemia.",
